# Fetched west workspace (~6.5 GB: NCS + add-on) — reproduced by bootstrap.sh.
# In a git worktree this may be a symlink to the main checkout's workspace, so
# ignore both the directory and the symlink form.
workspace/
/workspace

# Machine-local hooks, kept out of tree.
/tools/*.local

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/

# Local virtualenv; the runners resolve it themselves ($PY in
# tests/host/sources.sh), so it is never activated and never on PATH.
.venv/
# where `make tools-install` puts CodeChecker; the sca gate finds it via
# $CODECHECKER, so this one is never on PATH either.
.venv-sca/

# Build output. One root for the whole repo: every producer writes its own
# subdirectory under ./build (cdk-matter, nrf5340dk, esp32-<app>-<target>,
# host, _sig …), so `make clean` is a single rm and nothing is left behind.
# The unanchored form stays because calling idf.py directly inside an ESP app
# bypasses the shared root and writes that app's own build/.
/build/
build/
twister-out/
.west/

# Local bench config / secrets — J-Link serials, iPhone UDIDs, shell TTY.
# Nothing in the tree reads this yet; the rule is here so a scratch file by that
# name can never be committed by accident. Ship a bench.env.example alongside it
# if a target ever starts sourcing it.
bench.env

# Python build artifacts from an editable install of the HA agent
*.egg-info/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# claude
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.worktreeinclude

# codex
.codex/

# the built site. Generated output is never committed here: that is what made
# docs/ conflict on every merge, on derived lines no resolution could settle.
web/dist/
# emscripten output: 37 KB of minified JS on one line. Build it, never commit it.
web/twin/twin.js

# internal working notes / plans (not part of the project)
internal/

# BLE/UWB captures: they carry personal Bluetooth data (paired device names,
# nearby IDs, notification metadata) and must never be committed. Keep the
# dissector's real-capture testing out of the repo.
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.pklg
*.btsnoop
btsnoop_hci.log

# Flight-recorder traces and bench console logs. Same rule as the captures
# above, and for a sharper reason: a .frc carries the live ephemeral URSK,
# which is the key the whole unlock rests on.
# `make esp-lab` drops walkup-<timestamp>.log straight into the repo root.
*.frc
walkup-*.log
session.log
# `make monitor | tee` during a range_bias.py capture (tinyml repo). Only the
# parsed CSV is tracked.
clear*.log
blocked*.log

# scratchpad
scratchpad/

# video generation
video/

# Generated by scripts/ultrawidelock-enroll.py: holds a private credential key.
examples/zephyr/nrf5340dk-initiator/src/bench_identity.h

# Firecrawl
.firecrawl/

# HITL capture data: contains phone BLE addresses.
captures/

# Editor workspace
.cursor/

# graphify knowledge graph: generated, machine-local
graphify-out/
# where `make docs` installs graphify when it is not already on PATH
.venv-graphify/

# vendored renderers, fetched not committed
web/vendor/

# impeccable
.impeccable/
